---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Resources | Every Real Estate Calculator"
  description="Learn how real estate commission and fixed-rate mortgage estimates work, with USD examples, key terms, formulas and clear limitations."
  canonical="https://everyrealestatecalculator.com/resources/"
  bodyClass="resources-page"
  currentNav="resources"
  extraStyles={["../assets/resources.css"]}
>
<main id="main">
<section class="res-intro"><div class="wrap"><h1>Real Estate Resources</h1><p>Practical guides to buying, selling, financing and investing in real estate.</p></div></section>
<section class="res-guides" id="available-title" aria-label="Guides"><div class="wrap"><div class="article-grid">
<article class="article-card" id="mortgage-guide"><div class="article-card-top"><span class="chip">Mortgage</span></div><h2 id="mortgage-title">Understanding Mortgage Payments</h2><p class="article-card-desc">How a fixed-rate mortgage payment is calculated: principal, interest, the amortization formula, a worked example, and how taxes, insurance, HOA dues and PMI change the full monthly cost when you enter them.</p><div class="article-card-foot"><span class="read-time">3 min read</span><a class="read-link" aria-label="Read article: Understanding Mortgage Payments" href="mortgage-payments/">Read article <svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></div></article>
<article class="article-card" id="commission-guide"><div class="article-card-top"><span class="chip">For agents</span></div><h2 id="commission-title">Understanding Real Estate Commission</h2><p class="article-card-desc">How a sale price becomes an agent's earnings: gross commission, fees taken off the top, the split between listing and buyer sides, your share, and the transaction fee — with a worked example.</p><div class="article-card-foot"><span class="read-time">2 min read</span><a class="read-link" aria-label="Read article: Understanding Real Estate Commission" href="real-estate-commission/">Read article <svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></div></article>
<article class="article-card" id="affordability-guide"><div class="article-card-top"><span class="chip">Buying</span></div><h2 id="affordability-title">How Much House Can I Afford?</h2><p class="article-card-desc">Work out the home price your income supports: the 28/36 rule, front-end and back-end debt-to-income ratios, a worked example from income to maximum price, and what lenders actually allow.</p><div class="article-card-foot"><span class="read-time">8 min read</span><a class="read-link" aria-label="Read article: How Much House Can I Afford?" href="how-much-house-can-i-afford/">Read article <svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></div></article>
<article class="article-card" id="cap-rate-guide"><div class="article-card-top"><span class="chip">Investing</span></div><h2 id="cap-rate-title">What Is a Good Cap Rate?</h2><p class="article-card-desc">What counts as a good cap rate, and why there is no single number: the formula, a worked example, typical 2026 ranges by market type, and what the rate leaves out.</p><div class="article-card-foot"><span class="read-time">10 min read</span><a class="read-link" aria-label="Read article: What Is a Good Cap Rate?" href="what-is-a-good-cap-rate/">Read article <svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></div></article>
<article class="article-card" id="rent-vs-buy-guide"><div class="article-card-top"><span class="chip">Buying</span></div><h2 id="rent-vs-buy-title">Should I Rent or Buy a House?</h2><p class="article-card-desc">Rent or buy? Compare the full monthly cost of owning with rent, find the breakeven year, and test the 5% rule and price-to-rent ratio — with a worked example from the Rent vs Buy Calculator.</p><div class="article-card-foot"><span class="read-time">15 min read</span><a class="read-link" aria-label="Read article: Should I Rent or Buy a House?" href="should-i-rent-or-buy-a-house/">Read article <svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></div></article>
<article class="article-card" id="wholesale-guide"><div class="article-card-top"><span class="chip">Investing</span></div><h2 id="wholesale-title">The 70% Rule in Wholesale Real Estate</h2><p class="article-card-desc">How the 70% rule sets your maximum allowable offer on a wholesale deal: the formula, a worked example from the Wholesale Calculator, what the 30% covers, and when to adjust the percentage.</p><div class="article-card-foot"><span class="read-time">10 min read</span><a class="read-link" aria-label="Read article: The 70% Rule in Wholesale Real Estate" href="70-percent-rule/">Read article <svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></div></article>
</div></div></section>
<section class="res-directory" id="calculators"><div class="wrap">
<h2 id="reading-title">Every calculator, one click away</h2>
<p class="dir-intro">Grouped by the job at hand — buying, investing, selling, tax and agent work. For full descriptions and search, use the All Tools directory.</p>
<div class="dir-groups">
<div class="dir-group"><h3>Buying</h3><div class="dir-links"><a href="../tools/mortgage-calculator/">Mortgage</a><a href="../tools/home-affordability-calculator/">Home affordability</a><a href="../tools/rent-vs-buy-calculator/">Rent vs buy</a></div></div>
<div class="dir-group"><h3>Investing</h3><div class="dir-links"><a href="../tools/cap-rate-calculator/">Cap rate</a><a href="../tools/noi-calculator/">NOI</a><a href="../tools/roi-calculator/">ROI</a><a href="../tools/property-investment-calculator/">Property investment</a></div></div>
<div class="dir-group"><h3>Selling</h3><div class="dir-links"><a href="../tools/bridge-loan-calculator/">Bridge loan</a></div></div>
<div class="dir-group"><h3>Tax</h3><div class="dir-links"><a href="../tools/capital-gains-tax-calculator/">Capital gains tax</a></div></div>
<div class="dir-group"><h3>For agents</h3><div class="dir-links"><a href="../tools/commission-calculator/">Commission</a></div></div>
</div>
</div></section>
</main>
</BaseLayout>
